Package: vabaxos-voice
Architecture: all
Maintainer: VabaxOS <https://github.com/Vabax-dev/VabaxOS>
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Depends: python3, python3-numpy, python3-onnxruntime, libespeak-ng1, libsonic0, libpulse0, espeak-ng, speech-dispatcher, speech-dispatcher-espeak-ng, init-system-helpers
Description: Natural voices for VabaxOS (Kokoro)
 Kokoro, a natural-sounding neural voice, for Orca and every program that
 speaks through Speech Dispatcher (ADR-0019). At boot vabaxos-voice-select
 measures the computer: if it is fast enough, Kokoro becomes the desktop
 voice, with the fastest voice of each language; otherwise eSpeak NG stays.
 Speed comes from Sonic, so words stay clear when speaking fast. Phrases
 already said are cached, and speech stops at once on every key.
